## Current K3 Test Program

The current K3 test creates:

    the name server
    the clock server
    the clock notifier
    one idle task
    four clock client tasks

The four clock clients use the assignment parameters:

    priority 3, delay interval 10 ticks, number of delays 20
    priority 4, delay interval 23 ticks, number of delays 9
    priority 5, delay interval 33 ticks, number of delays 6
    priority 6, delay interval 71 ticks, number of delays 3

Each client obtains the clock server tid using WhoIs("clock"), then repeatedly calls Delay(). After each delay, it prints:

    its tid
    its delay interval
    the number of completed delays
    the current clock time

## Observed Test Output

The test output shows that:

    the name server starts
    the clock server registers as "clock"
    the notifier is created
    all four clients receive their configurations
    all four clients complete their requested delays
    the idle task continues running afterward

Observed completed client counts:

    delay 10: completed 20/20
    delay 23: completed 9/9
    delay 33: completed 6/6
    delay 71: completed 3/3

The idle task reports periodic idle output after all clock clients finish.

## Current Implementation Note

This version includes AwaitEvent(EVENT_TIMER), a clock notifier, a clock server, Delay(), DelayUntil(), Time(), clock clients, and an idle task.

The current timer event path is implemented using a software timer wait queue based on the ARM counter. The next improvement is to connect AwaitEvent(EVENT_TIMER) to a real hardware timer interrupt path.
